# [DD-13b.W1.3, D89 addendum point 3 + addendum 4(3)] THE FOUR CALL SHAPES,
# one target each, over ONE definition — so the only thing that differs
# between the four artifacts is the call, which is what makes comparing their
# emitted rows a comparison of the call forms and not of four patterns.
#
# `piece` exports two of its three groups. The third is unnamed and unread and
# is ERASED in every one of the four; the two exported ones are erased as well
# in `plaincall`, because the export list says what MAY be delivered and the
# composition decides what IS (addendum 4(1)).
target = plaincall
target = sitecall
target = selfcall
target = flatcall

pattern ^(?&piece)$
name plaincall

pattern ^(?&s=piece)$
name sitecall

pattern ^(?&=piece)$
name selfcall

pattern ^(?&*=piece)$
name flatcall

pattern (?<kept>a)(?<other>b)(c)
name piece
export kept, other
